Z||000000||BroCar 87||10-22-2000||08:53 PM||||I have a 1987 Coupe. There is no power anything. I mean stock as you can get, other than custom things I've added. Well I read that some fieros have a light up front and one in the rear trunks. I had neither. SO, I took the rear light out of my project car (84 SE) and *ta ding*. I know have a funtional rear trunk light  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg"> <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||10
Z||000001||mbramble||10-22-2000||09:19 PM||||How'd you get it to turn on/off??  I had a donor's trunk light but could not figure out how to wire it into anything to make it turn off when the trunk was closed.  Finally took an extra door pin switch, mounted it to the wall between the trunk and engine compartment so it would close when the lid closes, ran a fused 12V over to it, and then wired the light to the switch and ground.  Works really great.<P>To my basic coupe with nothing but AC and rear defroster I have added pw/pm/pl, courtesy lights in the footwells, trunk light, sunroof, turbo wheels, remote trunk opener, and an aereo fascia.  Like having a new car!!<p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 10-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||10-22-2000||09:35 PM||||Nothing like trying to find something in that dark pit at night. I know, I still need a new switch for mine.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||BroCar 87||10-22-2000||09:42 PM||||Well I wired it to a toggle switch on the dash... right were there should be a trunk release (I don't have one of those either).<P>So its half custom, and half stock  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg"> <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000004||Seanh||10-22-2000||10:38 PM||||The on/off lead for the trunk light is in the latch. That little thing tword the rear of the latch. When you depress it, the light goes off. Check to see if the wires going to the latch on the trunk (if any), see how many there are, if you have 4, you can make it work. Let me see if I can find anything more on it.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
